 ## Context
 
-- PR: !`gh pr view $ARGUMENTS --json number,url,title,state,isDraft,headRefName,baseRefName,headRefOid,mergeable,reviewDecision,author 2>&1`
-- Checks now: !`gh pr checks $ARGUMENTS 2>&1; echo "exit=$?"`
-- Local branch: !`git branch --show-current` · uncommitted files: !`git status --porcelain | wc -l | tr -d ' '`
+Take the PR number, URL or branch from the user's current request. If omitted, use the PR of
+the current branch. Pass an explicit selector as one quoted argument to `gh`; omit it when empty.
+Use Codex's available shell tool to collect the context below after reading this skill. These
+are actual tool calls, not command interpolation in the skill text. Record the checks command's
+exit status as well as its output. Respect the current session's permissions for all tool calls.
 
-`$ARGUMENTS` may be a PR number, a PR URL, a branch name, or empty (= the PR of the current branch).
+```text
+gh pr view <selector> --json number,url,title,state,isDraft,headRefName,baseRefName,headRefOid,mergeable,reviewDecision,author
+gh pr checks <selector>
+git branch --show-current
+git status --porcelain
+```
+Count the status entries for uncommitted files. Obtain this context before following the loop.
 
